  "body": "The existing incoming `shx-kanban-shx-bb-cli-untested` card combines bb emitter, CLI and Bash test obligations in a three-point estimate. This planning refinement proposes a reviewable eight-point breakdown: pure bb emitter tests3, CLI tests3, remaining Bash mutation gaps2. The first slice defines emitted text/forms, malformed-IR boundaries, supplied order, fallback reachability and intentional-mutation acceptance criteria. Child UUIDs are proposals in the body; no card/status/frontmatter/event transition or implementation is admitted.\n\nStacked on sync PR1 at exact accepted source `f4ee133dcf1650c7eafb623ef084f62417252477`. Planning head `698efc86a3749db0fdc4ce62e1dac2ec71f1f5a5` changes exactly eight planning/evidence paths. Existing source, tests, config, workflows and operational events are unchanged. Original card prefix/comments, receipt and reflection prefixes, and previous79 captures remain exact; all117 lossless captures match hashes/sizes. The current owning Receipt River154440f consumer validates all four owned typed rows and known kinds, without claiming the historical mixed ledger passes.\n\nThe explicit existing baseline `bin/analyze --strict` passed once at `44aa8ebe5ef491f4f6619edd7a0f03c811bd00a8`: all seven checks,19tests/46assertions/0failures. Its inherited deprecation output remains visible. Gate inputs are unchanged; no future implementation/mutation tests or repeat are claimed. Attributed accepted Rheosef3 private CLI build/help/authoritative EDN readback now pass,31cards/33unchanged fixture files; the native API retains the keyword gate/commands/cwd without executing that command or any transition. Initial failed probe and corrected successful probe are both retained; Node24 local preparation supplies no Node22 release qualification.\n\nQualified published Rheos artifact consumption remains held under EtaMu239. Native planning review, reviewed breakdown and lawful ready admission remain prerequisites. Automatic merge stays off; this PR is blocked pending qualification. No model/provider/runtime/shell effects, services, secrets, settings, source adoption, package publication or deployment operation is included.\n",
